# Soave-Redlich-Kwong (1972) residual Helmholtz energy Ar(n, V, T) with
# quadratic mixing rules; equivalent to yaeos SoaveRedlichKwong
# (implementations.f90:166-226): delta1 = 1, delta2 = 0.
# Units follow yaeos: R [bar L /(mol K)], Pc [bar], Tc [K], V [L].
# Thanks to capture-avoiding inlining, ntot can use the letter i.

model srk
target fortran
use yaeos__constants, only: R

variables
    n   nc
    V
    T

parameters
    Tc    nc
    Pc    nc
    w     nc
    kij   nc nc symmetric
    lij   nc nc symmetric

expressions
    m_i     = 0.48 + 1.574*w_i - 0.175*w_i^2
    ac_i    = 0.42748*R^2*Tc_i^2/Pc_i
    b_i     = 0.08664*R*Tc_i/Pc_i
    alpha_i = (1 + m_i*(1 - sqrt(T/Tc_i)))^2
    a_i     = ac_i*alpha_i
    ntot    = sum_i n_i
    bmix    = sum_i sum_j n_i*n_j*((b_i + b_j)/2.0)*(1.0 - lij_ij)/ntot
    D       = sum_i sum_j n_i*n_j*sqrt(a_i*a_j)*(1.0 - kij_ij)
    f       = log(1.0 + bmix/V)/bmix
    g       = R*log(1.0 - bmix/V)

function
    -ntot*g*T - D*f
